From 6223455459f6ac80c1347a67e6c82e5f1aa53922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Henderson <nathan.henderson@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 09:29:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tensilelite): preserve full-width TDM K offsets (#13274)

JIRA ID : ROCM-32046

## Motivation

TDM K-offset updates discard the product's high word and address carry,
which can produce an incorrect tensor or scale address.

## Technical Details

Use full-width multiplication and carry propagation for initial and tail
offsets, including shared-scale descriptors. Add a CPU regression test
for the emitted address arithmetic.

## Test Plan

Run CPU regressions, gfx1250 code generation and assembly, and GPU
arithmetic and full-output GEMM checks.

## Test Result

Pre-patch GPU arithmetic failed carry/overflow checks; patched
arithmetic passed. CPU and code-generation checks passed, with unchanged
SGPR usage in the compared kernels. Every MXFP8 output value matched the
CPU reference before and after, including forced split grids and a tail
shape. No hang was reproduced; the reported crash's cause remains
unconfirmed.

## Risk level

Medium: changes generated address arithmetic and uses an additional
temporary SGPR.
